Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||12-28-2000||06:29 PM||||MP3s are already as small as they're going to get.. unless you reduce the quality to 56k/sec or something. That's a lot less than cd quality, but it makes an average 3 minute song about 1.5mb, which is more managable especially for sending via email.<P>there are many other ways for sending mp3s though, email isn't exactly fast... and you can't resume if their connection drops halfway through downloading the email. Also, most ISPs only offer a 5mb mailbox anyway..<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
